<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50890" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭdŭo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		viduus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to deprive</i>, <i>bereave</i> of any
			thing (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civibus urbem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 571</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ornos foliis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 9, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arva pruinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 518</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitem pristino alimento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. Arb. 1, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regna (Plutonis) lumine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 601</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dexteram ense,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 866</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">penates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 385</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maritum amplexibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 154, 38</span></i>
			. —With <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">architectus ingeni viduatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 7, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orba pedum partim, manuum viduata vicissim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 840</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭdŭāta</span></b> ,
			ae, <i>adj. f.</i>, <i>bereft of her husband</i>, <i>widowed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Agrippina viduata morte Domitii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 5</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 31, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 16,
				30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux viduata taedis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>divorced</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Med. 581</span></i>
			.</div>
